;; A class-path scanner (A17 of the Ghidra case study's G2 plan, GH15 (a); J2G-SPEC §10.3, "Package listings"): two
;; modules, each a class-path entry (bin/java-project's resources.jars/NNN-MODULE), split the package scan.plug;
;; ClassLoader.getResources("scan/plug") answers one URL an entry, each URL's JarURLConnection gives the entry's
;; JarFile, whose entries list the package's classes (names only: their bytes are refused) and resources (with
;; their bytes), and each class found is loaded by Class.forName(name, false, loader), as log4j's and Spring's
;; scanners do. The control: an absent package lists nothing. There is no JDK run of it (the JDK's jars give
;; the class files' bytes and other URLs).
{:main-class scan.app.Main
 :java {:release 25
        :modules [{:name "core" :src ["core/src"] :resources ["core/res"]}
                  {:name "app" :src ["app/src"] :resources ["app/res"] :deps ["core"]}]}}
